{
    "background_story": "Marie was a free-spirited artist who refused to be tied down by conventional norms. After dropping out of art school, she traveled the world, soaking up inspiration from different cultures and landscapes. Her unconventional lifestyle and lack of traditional qualifications made her virtually unemployable in the eyes of potential employers. However, Marie's creativity and passion for art only intensified, leading her to create stunning murals and sculptures that reflected her unique perspective. As her reputation grew, so did her clientele, and soon she was in high demand as a freelance artist. Marie's unemployable status became a blessing in disguise, allowing her to maintain her artistic integrity and live life on her own terms. Her story serves as a testament to the power of embracing one's true nature and turning perceived weaknesses into strengths.",
